Action by Section Officer: 

The Section Officer will: 

(i) Scrutinise the note of the Dealing Officer; 
(ii) Dispose of routine cases, like obtaining information for draft reply to 
Parliament questions; sending reminders, etc.; 
(iii) Record, where necessary, a note setting out his own comments or 
suggestions; 
(iv) Submit the case to the higher officer; 
(v) Monitor the progress of the case to avoid delay; 
(vi) on return of the file, take action, like issue of communication, further 
examination, etc. 

